WEBVTT

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:35.890
<b>Book 2: The Snow Continues to Fall</b>

00:01:34.230 --> 00:01:38.480
Death is just an endless sleep, eh?

00:01:43.910 --> 00:01:45.240
Onee-chan...

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.170
Go, Sawa.

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:56.260
You... should live.

00:01:56.740 --> 00:02:00.680
I won't just give up! I can't!

00:02:03.610 --> 00:02:07.250
Sawa, stop. It's all right...

00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:12.800
I don't want to be alone again!

00:02:13.450 --> 00:02:18.790
Sawa... You're not alone anymore.

00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:20.840
Isn't that true?

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:32.630
No!

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:41.080
Everybody dies eventually. 
Today was that day for her.

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:42.940
I wouldn't be so sure.

00:02:54.330 --> 00:02:56.070
Stubborn girl...

00:02:56.670 --> 00:02:57.630
Yukimura!

00:02:58.970 --> 00:03:02.700
<i>And so, the woman's revenge was complete.</i>

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:09.210
<b>Episode 5: Confidential File 620: Divine Right</b>

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:12.670
A secret organization fighting anti-government 
forces... A woman's revenge...

00:03:13.650 --> 00:03:15.040
Too boring?

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:18.310
No, it's actually very creative,

00:03:18.310 --> 00:03:20.720
but the readers have a 
real thirst for romance.

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:26.710
They'd prefer something more... tawdry?

00:03:26.710 --> 00:03:27.930
Elena-san!

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:43.320
I-I'm so sorry! I must've done 
something to upset you...

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:44.740
What do I do?!

00:03:44.740 --> 00:03:49.940
As my ghost writer, you should 
be able to guess what's going on...

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:58.040
Yoshinobu-sama is thrilled that the 
snake problem has been dealt with.

00:03:58.420 --> 00:04:00.990
But in the two weeks since its resolution,

00:04:00.990 --> 00:04:04.260
there now seems to be an infestation of ants...

00:04:04.650 --> 00:04:10.310
And it seems as if Tsukishiro is
 leaving honey out to attract them.

00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:12.990
Weapons taken from our organization.

00:04:14.780 --> 00:04:19.900
We get near the castle in the middle 
of night when there are fewer guards...

00:04:20.730 --> 00:04:22.620
and then raise some hell.

00:04:23.770 --> 00:04:27.290
You're to retrieve the honey 
from these ants,

00:04:27.290 --> 00:04:29.200
find Tsukishiro, and...

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:32.290
I just don't care anymore.

00:04:34.180 --> 00:04:37.100
Our group's continuity has been confirmed.

00:04:37.100 --> 00:04:40.100
What's that got to do with me?

00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:43.420
You chose to live.

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:45.950
For that girl's sake.

00:04:56.490 --> 00:04:58.460
Ow, ow, ow...

00:04:58.910 --> 00:05:02.040
Aw, I messed up.

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:10.680
I'm still alive.

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:14.250
Okay! Let's start over.

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:16.750
Arriving

00:05:19.230 --> 00:05:23.780
From now on, you can use 
the organization for survival.

00:05:23.780 --> 00:05:27.760
Head back and get some rest 
for today. I'll be in touch.

00:05:41.180 --> 00:05:44.780
Nana, why did you choose me?

00:05:52.440 --> 00:05:54.590
Why me?

00:05:55.290 --> 00:05:58.040
Yes! This is great!

00:05:58.040 --> 00:06:01.040
Father -> Me

00:05:58.040 --> 00:06:01.040
Even if it's not really me

00:05:58.040 --> 00:06:01.380
I'm so excited! Hooray!

00:06:01.380 --> 00:06:02.940
Yes!

00:06:18.810 --> 00:06:21.840
I wonder if Onee-chan is okay.

00:06:27.380 --> 00:06:28.740
Are you okay?

00:06:29.620 --> 00:06:31.030
That must've hurt, huh?

00:06:31.030 --> 00:06:33.280
There, there, it's all right.

00:06:38.010 --> 00:06:39.930
Okay, say "ah."

00:06:40.590 --> 00:06:43.250
Do it just like I taught you, okay?

00:06:44.870 --> 00:06:47.940
Pain, pain, go away!

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:49.960
Pain go away!

00:07:04.810 --> 00:07:06.020
Welcome home!

00:07:07.190 --> 00:07:09.800
Hey, what would you like for dinner?

00:07:09.800 --> 00:07:12.490
Should I make the soup with onions tonight?

00:07:18.190 --> 00:07:20.370
Onee-chan, dinner's ready!

00:07:26.980 --> 00:07:31.060
You haven't eaten all day. 
You've gotta eat something.

00:07:31.450 --> 00:07:32.510
It's fine.

00:07:33.470 --> 00:07:36.360
What happened that one day?

00:07:37.900 --> 00:07:40.770
You won't tell me anything, but...

00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:44.260
Is it because I got taken 
by that bad person?

00:07:45.900 --> 00:07:48.570
Do your wounds hurt?

00:07:48.570 --> 00:07:52.230
Not really... I'm used to pain.

00:07:52.230 --> 00:07:56.030
There's no pain in this world 
you can truly get used to.

00:08:05.520 --> 00:08:07.750
I don't want to be alone again!

00:08:11.100 --> 00:08:14.400
I had an older brother.

00:08:15.410 --> 00:08:18.590
He was the type of person 
who would spend an entire day

00:08:18.590 --> 00:08:21.820
caring for an injured baby bird.

00:08:22.230 --> 00:08:24.630
He was very kind.

00:08:25.820 --> 00:08:30.280
But... he's gone now.

00:08:30.890 --> 00:08:33.500
My revenge is over.

00:08:36.740 --> 00:08:38.420
Aim for here.

00:08:39.380 --> 00:08:44.290
I'm prepared to face punishment 
for taking your loved ones away.

00:08:46.420 --> 00:08:49.800
Eat, then! Eat your poisoned food!

00:08:50.670 --> 00:08:52.950
If you feel bad, then eat!

00:09:01.310 --> 00:09:02.120
Here!

00:09:11.600 --> 00:09:13.570
You were lying, weren't you?

00:09:13.570 --> 00:09:16.320
Yeah, but I can poison you whenever I want.

00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:19.550
So you better eat every day! Okay?

00:09:37.840 --> 00:09:39.550
<b>Not Seeing Patients</b>

00:09:43.620 --> 00:09:44.520
Come in.

00:09:45.910 --> 00:09:48.120
Your ride's here.

00:09:50.700 --> 00:09:53.510
Didn't I tell you it's too soon to be
 fooling around with prosthetics?

00:09:53.510 --> 00:09:56.370
I'm less patient than I look.

00:09:56.370 --> 00:09:58.410
I can't wait for a whole year.

00:10:01.250 --> 00:10:04.630
Did you deliver my gift to your comrades?

00:10:04.630 --> 00:10:08.560
Yeah. I doubt they'll get 
through the walls easy,

00:10:08.560 --> 00:10:11.710
but they oughta at least 
be able to make a mess.

00:10:11.710 --> 00:10:13.640
It's very heroic.

00:10:13.640 --> 00:10:17.190
I would love to continue 
supporting your efforts, but...

00:10:17.190 --> 00:10:20.680
You're leaving Japan, right? 
For more freedom.

00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:24.080
Do you resent me for running?

00:10:25.070 --> 00:10:27.680
Ain't nothing wrong with running.

00:10:28.270 --> 00:10:30.490
Tell me one thing, though.

00:10:31.020 --> 00:10:33.680
Why help us?

00:10:33.680 --> 00:10:36.620
The way the Tokugawa sold 
your homeland off to foreigners

00:10:36.620 --> 00:10:41.650
and robbed you of your 
liberty is unacceptable.

00:10:41.650 --> 00:10:44.230
I wanted to lend a hand for your revenge.

00:10:44.230 --> 00:10:47.450
Revenge, huh? You might be right.

00:10:48.720 --> 00:10:52.080
Pursuing revenge, and being prepared 
to give your life for it...

00:10:57.010 --> 00:10:59.630
There's nothing more beautiful 
than a soul set on that.

00:11:00.330 --> 00:11:05.470
Especially for someone like me, 
who lost their chance at revenge.

00:11:07.140 --> 00:11:08.810
Something for the pain.

00:11:09.470 --> 00:11:13.450
They're hallucinogens, 
so don't go crazy with 'em.

00:11:14.160 --> 00:11:15.900
No need to worry.

00:11:15.900 --> 00:11:19.590
Another possible side effect 
is heart failure, y'know.

00:11:19.590 --> 00:11:21.390
I'm not going to die.

00:11:21.390 --> 00:11:23.480
Don't waste your life, you hear?

00:11:23.480 --> 00:11:27.540
You're not gonna get to visit your 
little bookstore if you're dead.

00:11:28.840 --> 00:11:31.250
It's... still open?

00:11:31.250 --> 00:11:34.440
Yeah. No real change, apparently.

00:11:40.700 --> 00:11:43.120
I will leave in private transport shortly.

00:11:43.120 --> 00:11:46.890
Best efforts will be made for 
the reconstruction of that hand.

00:11:47.790 --> 00:11:51.770
She's still alive... and still in a cage.

00:11:53.670 --> 00:11:57.220
And what of the blue jewel 
that was taken from the snake?

00:11:58.710 --> 00:12:03.780
Even we probably don't 
know the entire truth.

00:12:03.780 --> 00:12:06.780
It's the kind of thing that would spell 
the end if it got out in the open.

00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:11.490
An end to the Tokugawa 
regime, Nue... all of it.

00:12:13.580 --> 00:12:17.240
What happens to this country 
is none of my concern...

00:12:20.540 --> 00:12:25.840
But it seems I can't just abandon my 
role before it's time to leave the stage.

00:12:27.100 --> 00:12:30.050
The mission was a failure.

00:12:30.050 --> 00:12:32.870
Oh? That is not what we agreed upon.

00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:37.610
Yes... I am such a fool, it astounds me.

00:12:37.610 --> 00:12:42.640
What we want is the blue jewel 
created by the snake...

00:12:42.640 --> 00:12:47.370
However, we can make a trade 
for the gemstone, if it exists.

00:12:47.820 --> 00:12:50.990
Gemstone? I can't help you with that.

00:12:51.880 --> 00:12:53.750
You are a disappointment.

00:12:58.250 --> 00:13:02.520
You mean to tell me 
Tsuki has replaced Janome?

00:13:02.520 --> 00:13:07.350
Providing weapons to groups looking 
to overthrow the government

00:13:07.350 --> 00:13:08.510
poses enough of a threat.

00:13:10.420 --> 00:13:14.770
And you want me to get some 
intel out of this cutie here?

00:13:11.010 --> 00:13:14.770
<b>Background Information</b>

00:13:15.160 --> 00:13:17.020
You should be able to.

00:13:17.510 --> 00:13:18.600
Don't want to.

00:13:18.600 --> 00:13:19.430
What?

00:13:19.780 --> 00:13:21.220
Or more like, I can't.

00:13:23.450 --> 00:13:25.160
You're pregnant.

00:13:26.190 --> 00:13:29.380
You can tell? That's creepy.

00:13:29.810 --> 00:13:32.960
How could I not notice the difference?

00:13:33.310 --> 00:13:35.540
Fantastic.

00:13:35.540 --> 00:13:39.530
So, what now? Do I die?

00:13:52.800 --> 00:13:54.470
Let me go!

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:58.800
I told you, we've got pests to exterminate.

00:13:59.410 --> 00:14:01.360
I'm not going.

00:14:01.360 --> 00:14:03.980
Are you stupid? Just get a move on!

00:14:07.880 --> 00:14:08.870
Come on.

00:14:15.520 --> 00:14:16.970
You people...

00:14:17.600 --> 00:14:19.760
Tokugawa guard dogs?

00:14:19.760 --> 00:14:22.040
You'd be dead before you got inside.

00:14:22.040 --> 00:14:23.520
Maybe...

00:14:23.520 --> 00:14:25.410
But if we make a big enough fuss,

00:14:25.410 --> 00:14:29.460
it's gonna prove there are people 
who are fed up with the Tokugawa!

00:14:30.870 --> 00:14:32.300
In that case, dummy...

00:14:32.300 --> 00:14:34.890
You probably should've come during daytime!

00:14:41.290 --> 00:14:43.940
You're cuter than your picture.

00:14:46.970 --> 00:14:48.040
Don't mess with us!

00:14:48.040 --> 00:14:49.030
Kill them!

00:14:49.030 --> 00:14:50.200
Get 'em!

00:14:55.770 --> 00:14:57.200
Girl, over there!

00:15:01.070 --> 00:15:02.750
That's the last time, got it?!

00:15:03.710 --> 00:15:04.630
Yukimura!

00:15:14.930 --> 00:15:16.010
Sawa!

00:15:32.340 --> 00:15:33.900
What took you so long?!

00:15:50.310 --> 00:15:52.130
Oh, damn it!

00:15:52.130 --> 00:15:54.760
<b><i>Akadama</i></b>

00:15:56.510 --> 00:15:59.700
Ditching the job? You know that won't fly.

00:16:01.070 --> 00:16:04.060
I really hate you.

00:16:04.060 --> 00:16:06.650
You never say what you mean, 
you're a huge pain...

00:16:06.650 --> 00:16:10.280
But today's the last time, 
so I figured I'd pay you back.

00:16:14.330 --> 00:16:15.810
The last time?

00:16:15.810 --> 00:16:18.240
You're going to have new 
executioners to work with,

00:16:18.240 --> 00:16:20.360
replacing Tsukishiro and myself.

00:16:21.620 --> 00:16:24.340
I get to leave the organization.

00:16:24.340 --> 00:16:28.020
I've been granted a pardon 
by Yoshinobu-sama.

00:16:29.010 --> 00:16:33.600
Here. My new ID. 
I'm "May Yonezawa," apparently.

00:16:34.150 --> 00:16:36.700
Can you believe that? 
Me, a clerk at a trading company?

00:16:38.330 --> 00:16:39.810
What a joke.

00:16:39.810 --> 00:16:41.190
Is this real?

00:16:41.750 --> 00:16:46.140
As hard as it is to believe. 
Thanks to you killing Janome.

00:16:48.780 --> 00:16:50.230
Earlier, was that...

00:16:50.230 --> 00:16:54.210
Yeah. See, I hate lying.

00:16:54.880 --> 00:16:56.320
Are you actually going to have it?

00:16:57.160 --> 00:17:01.360
I kinda wished it would die, 
but seems it's pretty stubborn.

00:17:02.740 --> 00:17:05.570
And there's a certain idiotic man

00:17:05.570 --> 00:17:08.200
who wants to take care of it,

00:17:08.200 --> 00:17:10.360
even though he has no idea whose it is.

00:17:11.010 --> 00:17:13.690
I hate kids, personally.

00:17:13.690 --> 00:17:18.060
And the idea of "being someone's"... 
makes me want to puke.

00:17:19.250 --> 00:17:22.110
But I imagined something for the first time.

00:17:22.110 --> 00:17:24.270
A future that's different 
from what I have now.

00:17:24.780 --> 00:17:26.600
I don't understand.

00:17:26.600 --> 00:17:29.310
I don't expect you to.

00:17:29.310 --> 00:17:34.770
I don't care what anyone thinks. 
I know myself better than anyone.

00:17:37.810 --> 00:17:40.520
I'm going to choose how I live.

00:17:42.230 --> 00:17:46.030
Even people in a place like that should
 have that right, don't you think?

00:17:48.330 --> 00:17:51.330
Well, I'm just gonna enjoy life.

00:18:04.480 --> 00:18:07.440
I did say I hated you, remember?

00:18:07.940 --> 00:18:10.330
Don't trust anyone but yourself.

00:18:10.690 --> 00:18:14.980
And the next time you run... 
do it for real this time.

00:18:19.720 --> 00:18:22.060
I hate you, too!

00:19:01.330 --> 00:19:03.060
Said it was a murder-suicide.

00:19:03.060 --> 00:19:04.980
The woman set the fire.

00:19:04.980 --> 00:19:07.080
Scary...

00:19:37.480 --> 00:19:39.320
<i>Gone shopping</i>

00:19:43.060 --> 00:19:44.320
Why?

00:19:45.000 --> 00:19:49.080
She would never kill herself.

00:19:49.520 --> 00:19:52.460
Was she killed... to send a message?

00:19:53.470 --> 00:19:59.460
It was never really possible to 
leave the organization and live...

00:20:01.900 --> 00:20:04.410
Even though I've gotten 
revenge for my family,

00:20:04.410 --> 00:20:10.040
I'm going to have to keep 
fighting... but for what?

00:20:10.510 --> 00:20:13.980
I don't want to kill anyone anymore...

00:20:15.480 --> 00:20:19.750
But... if I run, Asahi and I will...

00:20:19.750 --> 00:20:20.930
What can I do?

00:20:20.930 --> 00:20:22.860
Then I can kill you.

00:20:26.510 --> 00:20:28.880
This time it will be for real.

00:20:28.880 --> 00:20:33.710
Tsukishiro-san gave this 
to me. It's real poison.

00:20:36.710 --> 00:20:40.150
So, Onee-chan... you have to die.

00:20:46.970 --> 00:20:50.230
If that's what you want...

00:20:58.340 --> 00:21:01.400
I didn't want to do this...

00:21:01.870 --> 00:21:04.540
I've always felt bad

00:21:04.540 --> 00:21:06.690
about upending your life...

00:21:08.890 --> 00:21:10.000
Onee-chan!

00:21:10.330 --> 00:21:12.830
Onee-chan! Onee-chan!

00:21:13.400 --> 00:21:17.620
If you're reborn... then next time...
